content.text:
Now set finalState when main_final is offered (both in onQuestComplete main_dungeon and init resume path). Better: inside `G.quests.offer` — no hook there. Simplest: in updateFinal, lazily create finalState if the quest is active:

```js
updateFinal(dt) {
  if (!this.finalState) {
    if (G.quests.activeIds.includes('main_final') && !G.quests.doneIds.includes('main_final')) {
      this.finalState = { spawned: false, warned: false };
    } else return;
  }
  ...
}
```

That handles both paths and loaded saves. Also on boss kill, main_final completes via quests.onKill (boss objective). And 'go' objective: fires via proximity — add in updateFinal after spawn: G.quests.onObjectiveFlag('main_final', 'go'). Then quest completes only after boss killed too (both objectives needed) — _checkComplete requires go>0 and boss count 1. Order: go first then boss — good.

Let me rewrite updateFinal accordingly.

