content.text:
I referenced `this.sheathSword` (a visual copy of the sword inside the sheath) and `this.arrows` — need to create them in buildBody. Also the weapon state needs initialization. Add to buildBody after sheath creation:

```js
// espada "guardada" (cópia estática dentro da bainha)
this.sheathSword = this.buildSword();
this.sheathSword.rotation.x = Math.PI; // invertida (punho para cima)
this.sheathSword.position.y = 0.05;
this.sheath.add(this.sheathSword);
```

And in constructor: `this.arrows = [];`

Also sheath is attached to hips which rotates with body — good.

Now update `update()` to call updateWeapon, and integrate with attacks: in handleAttack — if weaponType sword and weaponState !== 'drawn' → drawWeapon first (state 'attack' will restart after? Simpler: startAttack auto-draws instantly if needed and the draw delay is short: we set weaponState='drawing' and delay the swing by... complexity. Pragmatic: on startAttack, if weapon not drawn, draw it (0.45s) and DELAY the melee hit via attackHitDone timing — but the attack anim itself plays with the sword appearing mid-swing. Acceptable and cinematic: the draw happens DURING the wind-up. Since STATE_DUR.attack=0.42 > draw 0.45... close enough; visual shows sword appearing as swing starts. Good enough.

Also handleSpells: for mago casting, state 'cast' pose uses right arm — staff in hand. Fine.

Bow attack: in doMeleeHit, if weaponType() === 'bow' → doBowShot instead (spawn arrow, range from weapon.range||16, damage same formula). Mago: melee staff bonk with shorter reach (2.2).

