Now integrate into main.js startGame: for new game, show class selection instead of/after the intro dialog. Order: intro dialog first (Kael wakes up), then class selection? Actually class choice before the elder dialog makes the elder dialog reference the class. Simplest: show the class selection modal right at start (after the intro hint), and the elder dialog happens after selection (onEnd). But the elder dialog was a setTimeout(1200). Replace: for new game, after 800ms show openClassSelect(), and the elder dialog runs when class is chosen. But openClassSelect's onclick closes modal and returns; the elder dialog needs a hook — put it in the click handler? Cleaner: in main.js:

```js
if (!continuar) {
  setTimeout(() => { G.ui.openClassSelect(); }, 800);
  // elder dialog happens after class selection — check G.classe in a poll or move the elder dialog into class select onEnd
}
```

I'll add an onEnd callback param to openClassSelect(onEnd). Update panels accordingly. Also for continuar with saved class: player.weaponState should be 'drawn' if they had equipment. refreshEquipment handles visibility; set weaponState = 'drawn' on load if weapon equipped.

Also `Inventory.init()` currently auto-equips espada_ferro on new game — must NOT equip anymore (classes give items). Change init to only give the potion.

